    5. Build the OUTPUT grid: place bars at slots sorted by height ascending -> position left-to-right.
       This is the sorted/assembled state.
    6. Derive INPUT: for each slot, swap bar shapes back to their original (pre-sort) positions.
       Concretely: create a random permutation P of bar shapes, place shape P[i] at slot i
       with slot i's color. The output is the height-sorted version of this arrangement.
       Ensure the permutation is NOT already sorted by height (otherwise input == output).
